IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 145 -- INDEMNIFICATION OF OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES AND AGENTS; INSURANCE.
--
-- The section separates what a corporation MAY do (subsections (a), (b), (c)(2), (e), (g): "shall have power", "may be paid") from
-- what it MUST do (subsection (c)(1): "shall be indemnified"). One rule per relation: the person's claim (or privilege) and the
-- corporation's duty (or power) are the same relation, named neutrally; the seat layer words the question from the person's side.
-- Judgments the text hands to the person, the board or a court ("good faith", "reasonably believed", "reasonable cause", the
-- Court of Chancery's determination) are inputs. Cross-references taken as inputs: 10 Del. C. section 3114(b) (Title 10, not among the
-- inputs); section 251 and following (mergers, pieces dg6 to dg8); Title 18, chapter 69 (captive insurance, not among the inputs).
-- The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).

§ `Section 145(a): actions other than by or in the right of the corporation`

DECLARE `s 145 Kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `expenses (including attorneys' fees)`
    `judgments`
    `fines`
    `amounts paid in settlement`
    `an amount of any other kind`

DECLARE `s 145(a) Facts` HAS
    `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action, suit or proceeding is one by or in the right of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind of amount` IS A `s 145 Kind of amount`
    `the amount was actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action or proceeding is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had no reasonable cause to believe the person's conduct was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a): "A corporation shall have power to indemnify any person who was or is a party or is threatened to be made a party to any
-- threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative (other than an
-- action by or in the right of the corporation) by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent
-- of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another
-- corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise, against expenses (including attorneys' fees), judgments, fines
-- and amounts paid in settlement actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with such action, suit or proceeding
-- if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of
-- the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal action or proceeding, had no reasonable cause to believe the person's conduct
-- was unlawful." The four kinds of amount are the text's; an amount of any other kind is not covered.
-- src:436 | A corporation shall have power to indemnify any person who was or is a party or is threatened to be made a party to any threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative (other than an action by or in the right of the corporation) by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise, against expenses (including attorneys’ fees), judgments, fines and amounts paid in settlement actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with such action, suit or proceeding if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal action or proceeding, had no reasonable cause to believe the person’s conduct was unlawful. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(a) (src:436)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(a) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the kind of amount`
    WHEN `an amount of any other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        JUST (   f's `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative`
             AND (NOT f's `the action, suit or proceeding is one by or in the right of the corporation`)
             AND f's `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise`
             AND f's `the amount was actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the action, suit or proceeding`
             AND f's `the person acted in good faith`
             AND f's `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation`
             AND (   (NOT f's `the action or proceeding is criminal`)
                  OR f's `the person had no reasonable cause to believe the person's conduct was unlawful`))

DECLARE `s 145(a) Way a proceeding ended` IS ONE OF
    `by judgment`
    `by order`
    `by settlement`
    `by conviction`
    `upon a plea of nolo contendere or its equivalent`
    `in any other way`

-- "The termination of any action, suit or proceeding by judgment, order, settlement, conviction, or upon a plea of nolo contendere or
-- its equivalent, shall not, of itself, create a presumption that the person did not act in good faith and in a manner which the
-- person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal
-- action or proceeding, had reasonable cause to believe that the person's conduct was unlawful." The five ways are the text's.
-- src:436 | The termination of any action, suit or proceeding by judgment, order, settlement, conviction, or upon a plea of nolo contendere or its equivalent, shall not, of itself, create a presumption that the person did not act in good faith and in a manner which the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation, and, with respect to any criminal action or proceeding, had reasonable cause to believe that the person’s conduct was unlawful.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(a) (src:436)
GIVEN `the way the proceeding ended` IS A `s 145(a) Way a proceeding ended`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `the way the proceeding ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the proceeding ended`
    WHEN `in any other way` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 145(b): actions by or in the right of the corporation`

DECLARE `s 145(b) Facts` HAS
    `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit` IS A NUMBER
    `the person acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court of Chancery or the court in which the action or suit was brought has determined upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances, the person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expenses the court has deemed proper` IS A NUMBER

-- (b): power to indemnify "against expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection
-- with the defense or settlement of such action or suit if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably
-- believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation and except that no indemnification shall be made in
-- respect of any claim, issue or matter as to which such person shall have been adjudged to be liable to the corporation unless and
-- only to the extent that the Court of Chancery or the court in which such action or suit was brought shall determine upon application
-- that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances of the case, such person is fairly and reasonably
-- entitled to indemnity for such expenses which the Court of Chancery or such other court shall deem proper."
-- Only expenses (not judgments, fines or settlement amounts) are covered by (b). The carve-out: where the person was adjudged liable,
-- nothing unless and only to the extent the court so determines.
-- src:437 | A corporation shall have power to indemnify any person who was or is a party or is threatened to be made a party to any threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise against expenses (including attorneys’ fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of such action or suit if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation and except that no indemnification shall be made in respect of any claim, issue or matter as to which such person shall have been adjudged to be liable to the corporation unless and only to the extent that the Court of Chancery or the court in which such action or suit was brought shall determine upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances of the case, such person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for such expenses which the Court of Chancery or such other court shall deem proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(b) (src:437)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(b) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` f MEANS
        f's `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor`
    AND f's `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise`
    AND f's `the person acted in good faith`
    AND f's `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation`
    AND (   (NOT f's `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter`)
         OR f's `the Court of Chancery or the court in which the action or suit was brought has determined upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances, the person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses`)

-- The most the corporation has power to indemnify under (b), in dollars: the expenses actually and reasonably incurred, or, where the
-- person was adjudged liable, no more than the court has deemed proper. 0 where the power does not arise.
-- src:437 | against expenses (including attorneys’ fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of such action or suit if the person acted in good faith and in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation and except that no indemnification shall be made in respect of any claim, issue or matter as to which such person shall have been adjudged to be liable to the corporation unless and only to the extent that the Court of Chancery or the court in which such action or suit was brought shall determine upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances of the case, such person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for such expenses which the Court of Chancery or such other court shall deem proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(b) (src:437)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(b) Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` f MEANS
    IF   NOT (`s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` f)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   f's `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter`
         THEN minimum (LIST f's `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit`, f's `the expenses the court has deemed proper`)
         ELSE f's `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit`

§ `Section 145(c): success on the merits or otherwise`

-- "For indemnification with respect to any act or omission occurring after December 31, 2020".
-- src:438 | For indemnification with respect to any act or omission occurring after December 31, 2020, references to “officer” for purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (2) of this section shall mean only a person who at the time of such act or omission is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to § 3114(b) of Title 10 (for purposes of this sentence only, treating residents of this State as if they were nonresidents to apply § 3114(b) of Title 10 to this sentence).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(c)(1) (src:438)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 145(c)(1) December 31, 2020` MEANS YMD 2020 12 31

DECLARE `s 145(c) Facts` HAS
    `the person is a present or former director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE
-- out of range: 10 Del. C. section 3114(b) (Title 10, not among the inputs): whether the person is deemed to have consented is a plain fact.
    `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense` IS A NUMBER

-- "references to 'officer' for purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (2) of this section shall mean only a person who at the time of such act
-- or omission is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to
-- 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)": for an act or omission after 31 December 2020; for an earlier one the word has its ordinary meaning.
