@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(c)(1) (src:438)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(c) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` f MEANS
        f's `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation`
    AND (   (f's `the date of the act or omission` AT MOST `s 145(c)(1) December 31, 2020`)
         OR f's `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)`)

-- (c)(1): "To the extent that a present or former director or officer of a corporation has been successful on the merits or otherwise in
-- defense of any action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b) of this section, or in defense of any claim, issue or
-- matter therein, such person shall be indemnified against expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by
-- such person in connection therewith." A duty on the corporation; the person's claim.
-- src:438 | To the extent that a present or former director or officer of a corporation has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of any action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b) of this section, or in defense of any claim, issue or matter therein, such person shall be indemnified against expenses (including attorneys’ fees) actually and reasonably incurred by such person in connection therewith. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(c)(1) (src:438)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(c) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` f MEANS
        (   f's `the person is a present or former director of the corporation`
         OR `s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` f)
    AND f's `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein`

-- The amount of the claim under (c)(1), in dollars: the expenses actually and reasonably incurred. 0 where the duty does not arise.
-- src:438 | such person shall be indemnified against expenses (including attorneys’ fees) actually and reasonably incurred by such person in connection therewith. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(c)(1) (src:438)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(c) Facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 145(c)(1) the expenses the person must be indemnified against` f MEANS
    IF   `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` f
    THEN f's `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense`
    ELSE 0

-- (c)(2): "The corporation may indemnify any other person who is not a present or former director or officer of the corporation against
-- expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by such person to the extent such person has been successful on
-- the merits or otherwise in defense of any action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b) of this section, or in
-- defense of any claim, issue or matter therein." "Officer" is the narrowed word of the second sentence of (c)(1).
