@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(c)(2) (src:439)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(c) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `the person is a present or former director of the corporation`)
    AND (NOT (`s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` f))
    AND f's `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein`

§ `Section 145(d): the determination that indemnification is proper`

DECLARE `s 145(d) Who made the determination` IS ONE OF
    `a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum`
    `a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum`
    `independent legal counsel in a written opinion`
    `the stockholders`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `s 145(d) Facts` HAS
    `the indemnification is ordered by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a director or officer of the corporation at the time of the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination was made as authorized in the specific case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the determination is that the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `who made the determination` IS A `s 145(d) Who made the determination`
    `the committee was designated by majority vote of the directors who are not parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are no directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the directors who are not parties directed that independent legal counsel make the determination` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (d): "Any indemnification under subsections (a) and (b) of this section (unless ordered by a court) shall be made by the corporation
-- only as authorized in the specific case upon a determination that indemnification of the present or former director, officer,
-- employee or agent is proper in the circumstances because the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in
-- subsections (a) and (b) of this section. Such determination shall be made, with respect to a person who is a director or officer of
-- the corporation at the time of such determination: (1) By a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to such action, suit
-- or proceeding, even though less than a quorum; or (2) By a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such
-- directors, even though less than a quorum; or (3) If there are no such directors, or if such directors so direct, by independent legal
-- counsel in a written opinion; or (4) By the stockholders." Indemnification ordered by a court needs no determination. For a person
-- who is not a director or officer at the time, the text prescribes no method: the determination in the specific case suffices.
-- The answer is whether the indemnification may be made.
-- src:440 | (d) Any indemnification under subsections (a) and (b) of this section (unless ordered by a court) shall be made by the corporation only as authorized in the specific case upon a determination that indemnification of the present or former director, officer, employee or agent is proper in the circumstances because the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b) of this section. Such determination shall be made, with respect to a person who is a director or officer of the corporation at the time of such determination:
-- src:441 | (1) By a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to such action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum; or
-- src:442 | (2) By a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum; or
-- src:443 | (3) If there are no such directors, or if such directors so direct, by independent legal counsel in a written opinion; or
-- src:444 | (4) By the stockholders.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(d) (src:440-444)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(d) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the indemnification is ordered by a court`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE     f's `the determination was made as authorized in the specific case`
         AND f's `the determination is that the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b)`
         AND (   (NOT f's `the person is a director or officer of the corporation at the time of the determination`)
              OR (CONSIDER f's `who made the determination`
                  WHEN `a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum` THEN TRUE
                  WHEN `a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum` THEN f's `the committee was designated by majority vote of the directors who are not parties`
                  WHEN `independent legal counsel in a written opinion` THEN (   f's `there are no directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding`
                                                                              OR f's `the directors who are not parties directed that independent legal counsel make the determination`)
                  WHEN `the stockholders` THEN TRUE
                  WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE))

§ `Section 145(e): expenses paid in advance`

DECLARE `s 145(e) Facts` HAS
    `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (e): "Expenses (including attorneys' fees) incurred by an officer or director of the corporation in defending any civil, criminal,
-- administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding may be paid by the corporation in advance of the final disposition of such
-- action, suit or proceeding upon receipt of an undertaking by or on behalf of such director or officer to repay such amount if it shall
-- ultimately be determined that such person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section. Such
-- expenses (including attorneys' fees) incurred by former directors and officers or other employees and agents of the corporation or by
-- persons serving at the request of the corporation as directors, officers, employees or agents of another corporation, partnership,
-- joint venture, trust or other enterprise may be so paid upon such terms and conditions, if any, as the corporation deems appropriate."
-- A permission of the corporation ("may be paid"): a right to advancement exists only where a bylaw or agreement gives one (subsection (f)).
-- A present director or officer: on receipt of the undertaking. The others: on the terms the corporation deems appropriate (the text
-- requires no undertaking), so the answer is TRUE for them whether or not an undertaking was given.
-- src:445 | (e) Expenses (including attorneys’ fees) incurred by an officer or director of the corporation in defending any civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding may be paid by the corporation in advance of the final disposition of such action, suit or proceeding upon receipt of an undertaking by or on behalf of such director or officer to repay such amount if it shall ultimately be determined that such person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section. Such expenses (including attorneys’ fees) incurred by former directors and officers or other employees and agents of the corporation or by persons serving at the request of the corporation as directors, officers, employees or agents of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise may be so paid upon such terms and conditions, if any, as the corporation deems appropriate.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(e) (src:445)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(e) Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` f MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   f's `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation`
         THEN JUST (f's `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section`)
         ELSE IF   f's `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 145(f), (j) and (k): other rights, continuation, and the forum`

-- (f), first sentence: "The indemnification and advancement of expenses provided by, or granted pursuant to, the other subsections
-- of this section shall not be deemed exclusive of any other rights to which those seeking indemnification or advancement of expenses
-- may be entitled under any bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors or otherwise, both as to action in such
-- person's official capacity and as to action in another capacity while holding such office."
-- src:446 | The indemnification and advancement of expenses provided by, or granted pursuant to, the other subsections of this section shall not be deemed exclusive of any other rights to which those seeking indemnification or advancement of expenses may be entitled under any bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors or otherwise, both as to action in such person’s official capacity and as to action in another capacity while holding such office. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(f) (src:446)
GIVEN `the person has another right to indemnification or advancement of expenses under a bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(f) the other subsections of this section are the exclusive source of the person's rights` `the person has another right to indemnification or advancement of expenses under a bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors or otherwise` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (f), second sentence: "A right to indemnification or to advancement of expenses arising under a provision of the certificate of
-- incorporation or a bylaw shall not be eliminated or impaired by an amendment to or repeal or elimination of the certificate of
-- incorporation or the bylaws after the occurrence of the act or omission that is the subject of the civil, criminal, administrative or
-- investigative action, suit or proceeding for which indemnification or advancement of expenses is sought, unless the provision in
-- effect at the time of such act or omission explicitly authorizes such elimination or impairment after such action or omission has
-- occurred." TRUE: the right is protected. An amendment on the same day as the act is not "after" it (Fork F-145-1: dates only).
-- src:446 | A right to indemnification or to advancement of expenses arising under a provision of the certificate of incorporation or a bylaw shall not be eliminated or impaired by an amendment to or repeal or elimination of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws after the occurrence of the act or omission that is the subject of the civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding for which indemnification or advancement of expenses is sought, unless the provision in effect at the time of such act or omission explicitly authorizes such elimination or impairment after such action or omission has occurred.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(f) (src:446)
GIVEN `where the provision giving the right is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination` IS A DATE
      `the provision in effect at the time of the act or omission explicitly authorizes the elimination or impairment after the act or omission has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `where the provision giving the right is made` `the date of the act or omission` `the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination` `the provision in effect at the time of the act or omission explicitly authorizes the elimination or impairment after the act or omission has occurred` MEANS
        `dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the provision giving the right is made`
    AND (`the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination` GREATER THAN `the date of the act or omission`)
    AND (NOT `the provision in effect at the time of the act or omission explicitly authorizes the elimination or impairment after the act or omission has occurred`)

-- (j): "The indemnification and advancement of expenses provided by, or granted pursuant to, this section shall, unless otherwise
-- provided when authorized or ratified, continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent and shall
-- inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of such a person."
-- src:454 | (j) The indemnification and advancement of expenses provided by, or granted pursuant to, this section shall, unless otherwise provided when authorized or ratified, continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent and shall inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of such a person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(j) (src:454)
GIVEN `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent` `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified` MEANS
    NOT `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified`

-- src:454 | (j) The indemnification and advancement of expenses provided by, or granted pursuant to, this section shall, unless otherwise provided when authorized or ratified, continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent and shall inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of such a person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(j) (src:454)
GIVEN `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of the person` `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified` MEANS
    NOT `it was otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified`

-- (k): "The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine all actions for advancement of
-- expenses or indemnification brought under this section or under any bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested
-- directors, or otherwise. The Court of Chancery may summarily determine a corporation's obligation to advance expenses (including
-- attorneys' fees)."
