§ `Section 145(g): insurance`

-- (g), first sentence: "A corporation shall have power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of any person who is or was a
-- director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer,
-- employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise against any liability asserted against
-- such person and incurred by such person in any such capacity, or arising out of such person's status as such, whether or not the
-- corporation would have power to indemnify such person against such liability under this section."
-- src:447 | A corporation shall have power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of any person who is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise against any liability asserted against such person and incurred by such person in any such capacity, or arising out of such person’s status as such, whether or not the corporation would have the power to indemnify such person against such liability under this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(g) (src:447)
GIVEN `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation would have power to indemnify the person against the liability under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(g) the corporation has power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of the person` `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` `the corporation would have power to indemnify the person against the liability under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 145(g) Facts about insurance through a captive insurance company` HAS
    `the insurance is provided directly or indirectly by or through a captive insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the captive insurance company is organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of a jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms exclude coverage for, and provide that the insurer shall not pay, loss arising out of a personal profit or financial advantage to which the person was not legally entitled, or a deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act or a knowing violation of law, if established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding (not an action or proceeding to determine coverage), unless and only to the extent the person is entitled to be indemnified under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms require that a determination to make a payment in respect of a claim against a current director or officer be made by an independent claims administrator or in accordance with paragraphs (d)(1) through (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms require that, before a payment in connection with a dismissal or compromise of an action, suit or proceeding by or in the right of the corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, the corporation include in the notice that a payment is proposed to be made under the insurance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (g), captive insurance: "insurance shall include any insurance provided directly or indirectly (including pursuant to any fronting or
-- reinsurance arrangement) by or through a captive insurance company organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of any
-- jurisdiction, including any captive insurance company licensed under Chapter 69 of Title 18, provided that the terms of any such
-- captive insurance shall: (1) Exclude from coverage ...; (2) Require that any determination to make a payment ... ; and (3) Require
-- that, prior to any payment ...". Insurance not provided through a captive insurance company is insurance without these terms.
-- src:447 | For purposes of this subsection, insurance shall include any insurance provided directly or indirectly (including pursuant to any fronting or reinsurance arrangement) by or through a captive insurance company organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of any jurisdiction, including any captive insurance company licensed under Chapter 69 of Title 18, provided that the terms of any such captive insurance shall:
-- src:448 | (1) Exclude from coverage thereunder, and provide that the insurer shall not make any payment for, loss in connection with any claim made against any person arising out of, based upon or attributable to any (i) personal profit or other financial advantage to which such person was not legally entitled or (ii) deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act of such person, or a knowing violation of law by such person, if (in the case of the foregoing paragraph (g)(1)(i) or (ii) of this section) established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding in respect of such claim (which shall not include an action or proceeding initiated by the insurer or the insured to determine coverage under the policy), unless and only to the extent such person is entitled to be indemnified therefor under this section;
-- src:449 | (2) Require that any determination to make a payment under such insurance in respect of a claim against a current director or officer (as defined in paragraph (c)(1) of this section) of the corporation shall be made by a independent claims administrator or in accordance with the provisions of paragraphs (d)(1) through (4) of this section; and
-- src:450 | (3) Require that, prior to any payment under such insurance in connection with any dismissal or compromise of any action, suit or proceeding brought by or in the right of a corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, such corporation shall include in such notice that a payment is proposed to be made under such insurance in connection with such dismissal or compromise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(g) (src:447-450)
GIVEN f IS A `s 145(g) Facts about insurance through a captive insurance company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` f MEANS
    (NOT f's `the insurance is provided directly or indirectly by or through a captive insurance company`)
    OR (   f's `the captive insurance company is organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of a jurisdiction`
        AND f's `the terms exclude coverage for, and provide that the insurer shall not pay, loss arising out of a personal profit or financial advantage to which the person was not legally entitled, or a deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act or a knowing violation of law, if established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding (not an action or proceeding to determine coverage), unless and only to the extent the person is entitled to be indemnified under this section`
        AND f's `the terms require that a determination to make a payment in respect of a claim against a current director or officer be made by an independent claims administrator or in accordance with paragraphs (d)(1) through (4)`
        AND f's `the terms require that, before a payment in connection with a dismissal or compromise of an action, suit or proceeding by or in the right of the corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, the corporation include in the notice that a payment is proposed to be made under the insurance`)

-- (g), last paragraph: "For purposes of paragraph (g)(1) of this section, the conduct of an insured person shall not be imputed to any
-- other insured person. A corporation that establishes or maintains a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this
-- section shall not, solely by virtue thereof, be subject to the provisions of Title 18."
-- src:451 | For purposes of paragraph (g)(1) of this section, the conduct of an insured person shall not be imputed to any other insured person. A corporation that establishes or maintains a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this section shall not, solely by virtue thereof, be subject to the provisions of Title 18.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(g) (src:451)
GIVEN `the conduct is the conduct of another insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(g) the conduct of an insured person is imputed to another insured person for the purposes of paragraph (g)(1)` `the conduct is the conduct of another insured person` MEANS
    FALSE

-- out of range: Title 18 (not among the inputs): the rule says the corporation is not subject to it solely for this reason; what Title 18 requires is not read.
-- src:451 | A corporation that establishes or maintains a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this section shall not, solely by virtue thereof, be subject to the provisions of Title 18.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(g) (src:451)
GIVEN `the corporation establishes or maintains a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 145(g) the corporation is, solely by virtue of the captive insurance company, subject to the provisions of Title 18` `the corporation establishes or maintains a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this section` MEANS
    FALSE

§ `Section 145(h) and (i): constituent corporations, and employee benefit plans`

-- (h): "references to 'the corporation' shall include, in addition to the resulting corporation, any constituent corporation (including any
-- constituent of a constituent) absorbed in a consolidation or merger which, if its separate existence had continued, would have had
-- power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents, so that any person who is or was a director,
-- officer, employee or agent of such constituent corporation, or is or was serving at the request of such constituent corporation as a
-- director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise, shall stand in
-- the same position under this section with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation as such person would have with respect
-- to such constituent corporation if its separate existence had continued."
-- src:452 | (h) For purposes of this section, references to “the corporation” shall include, in addition to the resulting corporation, any constituent corporation (including any constituent of a constituent) absorbed in a consolidation or merger which, if its separate existence had continued, would have had power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents, so that any person who is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of such constituent corporation, or is or was serving at the request of such constituent corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise, shall stand in the same position under this section with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation as such person would have with respect to such constituent corporation if its separate existence had continued.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(h) (src:452)
GIVEN `the corporation the person served was a constituent corporation, or a constituent of a constituent, absorbed in a consolidation or merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that constituent corporation, if its separate existence had continued, would have had power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of that constituent corporation, or serving at its request as such of another enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(h) the person stands in the same position with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation` `the corporation the person served was a constituent corporation, or a constituent of a constituent, absorbed in a consolidation or merger` `that constituent corporation, if its separate existence had continued, would have had power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents` `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of that constituent corporation, or serving at its request as such of another enterprise` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation the person served was a constituent corporation, or a constituent of a constituent, absorbed in a consolidation or merger`
         AND `that constituent corporation, if its separate existence had continued, would have had power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents`
         AND `the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of that constituent corporation, or serving at its request as such of another enterprise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 145(i) Employee benefit plan matter` IS ONE OF
    `an employee benefit plan, as an other enterprise`
    `an excise tax assessed on a person with respect to an employee benefit plan, as a fine`
    `service as a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation which imposes duties on, or involves services by, the person with respect to an employee benefit plan, its participants or beneficiaries, as serving at the request of the corporation`
    `anything else`

-- (i): "references to 'other enterprises' shall include employee benefit plans; references to 'fines' shall include any excise taxes
-- assessed on a person with respect to any employee benefit plan; and references to 'serving at the request of the corporation' shall
-- include any service as a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation which imposes duties on, or involves services by,
-- such director, officer, employee or agent with respect to an employee benefit plan, its participants or beneficiaries". "Shall include"
-- adds to the ordinary meaning; it does not close it, so a matter of another kind is not covered.
-- src:453 | For purposes of this section, references to “other enterprises” shall include employee benefit plans; references to “fines” shall include any excise taxes assessed on a person with respect to any employee benefit plan; and references to “serving at the request of the corporation” shall include any service as a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation which imposes duties on, or involves services by, such director, officer, employee or agent with respect to an employee benefit plan, its participants or beneficiaries; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(i) (src:453)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 145(i) Employee benefit plan matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (i): "and a person who acted in good faith and in a manner such person reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants
-- and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan shall be deemed to have acted in a manner 'not opposed to the best interests of the
-- corporation' as referred to in this section." Otherwise the text does not say.
-- src:453 | and a person who acted in good faith and in a manner such person reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan shall be deemed to have acted in a manner “not opposed to the best interests of the corporation” as referred to in this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 145(i) (src:453)
GIVEN `the person acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(i) the person is deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` `the person acted in good faith` `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan` MEANS
    IF   `the person acted in good faith` AND `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
